Operator: model choice is driven by deployment fit, not speed/accuracy. The ARC Prize Kaggle validation
environment has 16GB VRAM and the model must fit WITH adequate KV cache for the interactive ARC-AGI-3
harness. Verified by du: gemma-4-12B Q4_K_M = 6.7GB -> ~9.3GB free for KV cache on a 16GB card (FITS).
Qwopus-27B and DiffusionGemma-26B Q4 = 16.8GB each -> weights alone exceed 16GB (do NOT fit). So
gemma-4-12B is the only deployable model of the three; the 27B models are offline-dev/research-only. This
supersedes the speed/accuracy comparison for the submission. Added the DECISIVE-constraint section to the
3-way comparison note. (Memory: project_kaggle_16gb_gemma12b.)

